<body class="py-14 px-8">
<div class="prose mx-auto">
    <h1 class="!mb-0">11ty Plugin: Vidyard</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="https://npmjs.com/package/eleventy-plugin-vidyard">
            <span class="sr-only">npm</span>
            <img class="inline-block !my-0" src="https://img.shields.io/npm/v/eleventy-plugin-vidyard.svg" alt="npm">
        </a>
        <a href="https://npmjs.com/package/eleventy-plugin-vidyard">
            <span class="sr-only">npm</span>
            <img class="inline-block !my-0" src="https://img.shields.io/npm/dt/eleventy-plugin-vidyard.svg" alt="npm">
        </a>
        <a href="https://npmjs.com/package/eleventy-plugin-vidyard">
            <span class="sr-only">license</span>
            <img class="inline-block !my-0" src="https://img.shields.io/npm/l/eleventy-plugin-vidyard.svg" alt="license">
        </a>
    </p>
    <p><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/eleventy-plugin-vidyard">This plugin</a> adds a shortcode to your Eleventy project to easily embed <a href="https://www.vidyard.com">Vidyard</a> videos using the Vidyard Player API v4.</p>
    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <p>Install the plugin from npm:</p>
    <pre><code>npm install eleventy-plugin-vidyard --save-dev</code></pre>
    <h2>Configuration</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><code>script</code> - Include the Vidyard embed script.<br/><small>Default: <code>true</code></small></li>
        <li><code>class</code> - The class attribute for the player image.<br/><small>Default: <code>vidyard-player-embed</code></small></li>
        <li><code>version</code> - The Vidyard API version.<br/><small>Default: <code>4</code></small></li>
        <li><code>type</code> - The player type.<br/><small>Default: <code>inline</code></small></li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Usage</h2>
    <p>Add it to your <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/docs/config/">Eleventy Config</a> config file:</p>
    <h3>ESM (Eleventy 3.0+)</h3>
    <pre><code>import eleventyPluginVidyard from 'eleventy-plugin-vidyard';

export default function (eleventyConfig) {
    eleventyConfig.addPlugin(eleventyPluginVidyard);
};</code></pre>
    <h3>CommonJS (Eleventy 2.x)</h3>
    <pre><code>const eleventyPluginVidyard = require('eleventy-plugin-vidyard');

module.exports = function (eleventyConfig) {
    eleventyConfig.addPlugin(eleventyPluginVidyard);
};</code></pre>
    <h3>Advanced usage:</h3>
    <pre><code>import eleventyPluginVidyard from 'eleventy-plugin-vidyard';

export default function (eleventyConfig) {
    eleventyConfig.addPlugin(eleventyPluginVidyard, {
        script: true,
        class: 'vidyard-player-embed',
        version: 4,
        type: 'inline'
    });
};</code></pre>
    <h3>Template usage (Nunjucks):</h3>
    <pre><code>&#123;% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/VIDEO_ID" %&#125;

{# With options #}
&#123;% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/VIDEO_ID", { script: false, class: "custom-class" } %&#125;</code></pre>
    <h3>Template usage (Liquid):</h3>
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Liquid templates don't support passing objects. Pass extra classes as a string instead:</p>
    <pre><code>&#123;% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/VIDEO_ID" %&#125;

{# With extra classes (appended to default class) #}
&#123;% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/VIDEO_ID" "my-custom-class" %&#125;</code></pre>
    <p><a href="/test-liquid/">View Liquid template demo →</a></p>
    <h2>Demo</h2>
    <h3>Basic Embed</h3>
    <div class="not-prose">
        {% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/Cse5Fqy1CpUWqYdtikKrFy?embeded=true", { script: false } %}
    </div>
    <h3>Custom Options</h3>
    <p>You can pass options directly to the shortcode:</p>
    <pre><code>&#123;% vidyard "https://share.vidyard.com/watch/VIDEO_ID", {
    script: false,
    class: 'vidyard-player-embed my-custom-class'
} %&#125;</code></pre>
    <h2>Custom Usage</h2>
    <p>Vidyard documentation recommends placing the script tag in the head of your page. In that case, disable script rendering in the shortcode:</p>
    <pre><code>&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;script src="https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js" type="text/javascript" async&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>And configure the plugin:</p>
    <pre><code>eleventyConfig.addPlugin(eleventyPluginVidyard, {
    script: false
});</code></pre>
